      ],
      "source": "https://www.wvencyclopedia.org/entries/1390",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1852 the town was renamed Aracoma after the eldest daughter of Shawnee chief Cornstalk, who lived there in 1765.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Logan-West-Virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Logan sits where the Guyandotte River meets Island Creek, a spot that helped fuel its coal‑mining boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
